course: dictionary
lesson: 10823
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it, which is its context. «A drip gives fluids or medicines straight into a vein.» Medicine goes into the body, so vein here means a tube in the body.
explain: «Leaf insects are flat and green with leaf veins.» Leaves do not have a blood tube, so vein here means a thin line in a leaf. Ask yourself where the word is and what is around it. The place tells you the meaning.
explain: Some words sit in phrases. «In the same vein» does not mean a tube or a line at all. It means in the same style or way, so you can guess it from the rest of the sentence and check it by swapping in your meaning.
fact: A vein is a tube in the body that carries blood back to the heart.
fact: A vein is a thin line on a leaf or an insect wing.
fact: A vein is a thin layer of a mineral or metal in rock, like «a vein of gold».
fact: Arteries carry blood away from the heart, while veins carry it back.
fact: «In the same vein» means in the same style or way.
exercise: «An anaesthetist watches the patient through a cannula, a thin plastic tube in a vein.» What is a vein in this sentence? | A part of a car engine | A thin layer of gold in rock | A thin line on a leaf | *A tube in the body that carries blood back to the heart
exercise: «Leaf insects are flat and green with leaf veins.» What is a leaf vein? | A kind of leaf insect | *A thin line in a leaf | A blood tube in a leaf | A small crack in the ground
exercise: Nadia says «in the same vein» is about gold. What does the phrase mean? | A thin line on a leaf | A thin layer of gold in rock | *In the same style or way | A tube carrying blood
test: «Blood is never blue: veins only look blue because of the way skin lets light through.» Why do veins look blue? | Because blood is blue | *Because of the way skin lets light through | Because the heart paints them | Because veins carry blue water
test: Mum says, «The drip gives fluids straight into a vein.» Where do the fluids go? | Into a rock full of gold | Into a leaf | Onto the skin | *Into a tube in the body that carries blood back to the heart
exam: «Miners followed a vein of gold through the rock.» What does vein mean here? | A thin line on a leaf | A way of doing something, in the same style | *A thin layer of metal in rock | A tube in the body
